# The north-star model

The project should aim to make this executable:

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{source text or movie}
\rightarrow
\mathcal S
\\
&\text{raw recall transcript/audio}
\rightarrow
\mathcal L_R
\\
&(\mathcal L_R,\mathcal S)
\rightarrow
p(C,\Psi,Q,R,Z,M,\Pi\mid X,\mathcal S)
\\
&\rightarrow
\text{segmentation-marginalized recall signatures}
\\
&\rightarrow
\text{population and neural estimands with propagated uncertainty}.
\end{aligned}
}
\]

That would be meaningfully beyond the cited systems.

It would not merely score whether a story event was “kind of mentioned.” It would model:

- what the person claimed;
- which words expressed it;
- what source structure it referred to;
- at what grain;
- with what precision;
- with which participants and relations preserved;
- where the recall jumped next;
- what came from outside;
- what interpretation remains uncertain;
- and whether the scientific conclusion survives that uncertainty.

That is the standard capable of making `storymodel4s` not just more elaborate, but demonstrably better.
